Zero-copy display: the flush of a host blob scanout carries a fence and the plane
update waits for it, as for a dumb buffer, when the module parameter
blob_flush_fence is set (default 0). The host completes that fence when its
compositor released the buffer shown before, so the guest does not render into
a buffer the host still shows.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-01 00:58:24.106434164 +0200
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_display.c	2026-10-01 00:58:49.347014865 +0200
@@ -83,6 +83,17 @@
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(flip_grace_us, "A flip this long after the host's vblank tick still completes for that tick (default 1200)");
 module_param_named(flip_grace_us, virtio_gpu_modparam_flip_grace_us, int, 0644);
 
+/*
+ * Zero copy: the host puts the scanout buffer itself on its screen, and it
+ * completes the flush of a frame only when its compositor released the
+ * buffer shown before, so the flush of a host blob carries a fence and the
+ * plane update waits for it (as for a dumb buffer), which keeps the guest
+ * from rendering into a buffer the host still shows.
+ */
+int virtio_gpu_modparam_blob_flush_fence;
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(blob_flush_fence, "Fence the flush of host blob scanouts too and wait for it (zero-copy display, default 0)");
+module_param_named(blob_flush_fence, virtio_gpu_modparam_blob_flush_fence, int, 0644);
+
